  "behavior": {
    "factory": "Private writer-new returns a canonical readable and a core writer integer; only private functions accept that integer. No public native factory/writer API is exposed.",
    "composition": "Instantiate the same helper package separately for reader and writer, with identical original resource aliases; avoid Wasmtime intra-instance nonnumeric read/write rejection. All memory and instances count toward existing Store limits.",
    "write": "Bounded canonical list lowering, native signal waitable, backpressure, status/count and remaining-payload packet lifted before original storage is reclaimed.",
    "ownership": "Transferred prefix belongs to the reader; unconsumed suffix returns as owned canonical values. Cancellation returns the unwritten owner for retry; peer closure returns it for disposal; original host destructor runs exactly once per owner.",
    "future": "Successful or peer-closed writes release the writable end. Cancelled unwritten future writers remain valid for retry; producer abort must retire the Store instead of dropping an unwritten writer against an open reader.",
    "stream": "Partial writes return the remainder; detach retained writable ends from the task waitable set before destroying the set. Explicit writable close produces reader EOF; unit streams preserve counts.",
    "memory": "Shared canonical metadata/allocator/cleanup, Unicode and 65,537 byte compound payloads, repeated future exchanges reach a memory-page plateau.",
    "nativeReaderRegression": "All 119 parent engine tests continue passing in both development and production panic-abort profiles, including native read/close/transfer and deterministic close races."
  },
